    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Verifies that substitution can produce output identical to its input. <p>The lookup map is arranged so that resolving {@code ${animal}} yields a string that, after all escaping and nested substitution is applied, reconstructs the original {@code ${animal}} literal: <ol> <li>{@code animal} → {@code \"$${${thing}}\"}</li> <li>{@code thing} → {@code \"animal\"}</li> <li>Inner substitution: {@code ${thing}} → {@code \"animal\"}, giving {@code \"$$\" + \"{animal}\"} → {@code \"$${animal}\"}</li> <li>{@code \"$$\"} is the escape sequence for a literal {@code \"$\"}, so the final value is the string {@code \"${animal}\"} — identical to the original placeholder.</li> </ol> <p>As a result, the full template {@code \"The ${animal} jumps.\"} is returned unchanged."
   },
